{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I charged you at that time all the things that you should do</b> — these are the ten matters that range from laws of monetary disputes to laws of capital cases. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 1:18), from Sifrei (on Deuteronomy 18). If so, He is speaking about the judges mentioned, and He abbreviates in ten matters, all of which are derived from the verses. And according to the plain sense, they are the statutes and the teachings — the way in which they should walk and the deed that they should do — for he commands and admonishes and teaches everything to Israel from His mouth. And the reason for mentioning this here is that it is well known that this matter was the advice of Jethro, for he said to Moses (Exodus 18:19), 'Be you for the people before Elohim' — that he should pray on their behalf in their time of distress — and he said to him (Exodus 18:20), 'And you shall admonish them with the statutes and the teachings,' etc. — that he himself should teach them the Torah. But regarding judgment he gave him advice that he should appoint judges to assist him, and I have already explained this there (Ramban on Deuteronomy 1:20). Therefore he recounted here that when he appointed the officers of thousands and hundreds, he appointed them only for judgment, but he himself would teach them all the things that they should do according to the Torah, for he heeded the advice of his father-in-law and did everything that he said. And Moses did not mention his advice here, nor did he say anything in the name of Jethro that he had said. And it appears to me that he did not wish to mention it in the presence of all Israel, out of his humility, or lest it not be to his honor to mention to this generation that he had taken a Cushite woman (Numbers 12:1). And it is possible that the reason is because he consulted the Shekhinah, and by authority of the Gevurah that matter was carried out:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The citation 'Ramban on Deuteronomy 1:20' appears in the source as a cross-reference; the verse number may be a copyist's error for Exodus 18, where the Jethro narrative is discussed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:43:59.970424338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}